WEBVTT

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:14.100
-Here's the rest!
-(PANTING)

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:19.460
(GLASS TINKLING, SHATTERING)

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:28.940
(PANTING, GRUNTING)

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:37.340
Excuse me, ma'am, but I believe
you're on the wrong flight.

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:39.380
-Woody!
-Come on, Jess.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:41.340
-It's time to take you home.
-But

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:43.540
-what if Andy doesn't like me?
-Nonsense!

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:45.660
Andy'll love you! Besides,

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:48.020
-he's got a little sister.
-He does?

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.740
-Why didn't you say so? Let's go!
-Whoa!

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:57.740
MAN: Hold it! There's a couple
more bags coming from the terminal!

00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:59.700
Okay. On three.

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:02.380
-One, two...
-Too late!

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:04.380
Put 'em on the next flight!

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:13.900
-This is bad.
-How are we gonna get outta here?

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:15.020
(LATCH CLICKS)

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:17.580
Over there! Come on!

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:28.180
(GRUNTING)

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:33.700
-You sure about this?
-No! Let's go!

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:51.100
(BOTH GASP)

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:56.500
-(YELLING)
-Hold on, Woody!

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:59.060
-(RIPPING SOUND)
-(YELLING)

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:04.380
-What's a cowboy without his hat?
-Buzz!

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.660
-(ENGINES ACCELERATING)
-(WHIMPERING)

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:20.740
Buzz! Buzz, get behind the tires!

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:24.620
(PANTING, GRUNTING)

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:28.540
Jessie, let go of the plane!

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:29.940
What? Are you crazy?

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:33.180
Just pretend it's
the final episode of Woody's Roundup.

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:36.780
But it was canceled!
We never saw if you made it!

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:38.780
Well, then, let's find out together!

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:41.980
(BOTH SCREAMING)

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:45.660
Oh-oh-oh.

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:55.660
-We did it! We did it! We did it!
-(LAUGHING)

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:57.220
Nice ropin', cowboy.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:59.980
That was definitely
Woody's finest hour!

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:02.260
-(LAUGHING)
-Your hat, partner.

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:05.260
-Hoo-hoo!
-(ENGINES ROARING)

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:10.540
Let's go home.

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:18.660
Yee-haw!

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:20.860
(PANTING)

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:23.460
(HUMS LONE RANGER THEME)

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:28.660
Hey, Woody! Woody?

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:37.380
Oh, wow! New toys!

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:39.500
Cool! Thanks, Mom!

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:43.060
It's Bazooka Jane
and her jet-propelled horse!

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:44.300
(MAKES JET SOUNDS)

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:48.060
Woody, Buzz, that polecat Zurg
has stolen my space cows!

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:49.820
(CONTINUES, INDISTINCT)

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:59.540
Andy, come on, hon. Time to go.

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:02.340
-Hey, you fixed Woody!
-Yeah.

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:06.700
Glad I decided not to take him to camp.
His whole arm might have come off.

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:14.180
Well, what do you know?

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:16.460
Yee-haw!

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:17.940
Oh, Bullseye,

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:20.620
we're part of a family again!

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:23.580
Hmm?

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:27.660
Uh, ma'am, I, uh... (CLEARS THROAT)

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:29.780
I wanted to say
you're a bright young woman

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:31.740
with a beautiful "yarnful" of hair.

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:34.580
"Hairful" of yarn. It's, uh...
Whoo... Uh...

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:36.140
(CLEARS THROAT) I must go.

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:39.780
Well, aren't you the sweetest
space toy I ever met?

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:41.980
(BARKING)

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:44.340
-What's that? Bark, bark?
-(BARKING)

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:48.020
This fella says he needs to go out
back for a little private time.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:49.940
That critter needs help!

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:55.660
♪ Yodel-ay-hee-hoo ♪

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:58.260
-(GRUNTS)
-(BARKS)

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:01.660
Ooh, ooh, oh...

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:03.620
Hey, Rex,
I could use a hand over here, buddy.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:06.540
I don't need to play. I've lived it!

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:09.220
-No, no, no, no! Oh, nuts!
-(CLICKS CHANNEL)

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:11.380
(WEEPING) Welcome to Al's Toy Barn.

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:14.220
We've got the lowest prices in town.

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:18.900
Everything for a buck, buck, buck.
(SOBBING)

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:22.340
Well, I guess crime doesn't pay.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:25.700
Oh, Andy did a great job, huh?
Nice and strong!

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:29.380
-I like it. Makes you look tough.
-(GIGGLES)

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:30.780
-(SMOOCHING)
-(LAUGHING)

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:33.620
You have saved our lives.
We are eternally grateful.

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:37.660
You saved their lives? Oh, my hero!

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:41.300
And they're so adorable!
Let's adopt them!

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:42.540
Daddy!

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:44.620
-Oh, no.
-(SQUEAKING)

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:47.620
Wheezy, you're fixed!

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:52.020
Oh, yeah. Mr. Shark looked in the toy
box and found me an extra squeaker.

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:55.180
-And how do you feel?
-Oh, I feel swell.

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:59.740
In fact, I think I feel a song
comin' on.

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:01.500
(BIG BAND MUSIC PLAYS)

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:05.100
ROBERT GOULET'S VOICE:
♪ You've got a friend in me

00:06:06.460 --> 00:06:09.260
♪ You've got a friend in me

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:12.900
♪ You just remember
what your old pal said

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:15.980
-♪ Babe, you've got a friend in me
-(BARKING)

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:19.380
-(GIGGLING)
-♪ Yeah, you've got a friend in me ♪

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:22.900
Come on over.
Oh, you are such a big girl.

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:25.060
Andy, you think she's ready
to drive the car yet?

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:26.900
-Yeah, and I can teach her.
-(BARKING)

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:29.820
-You still worried?
-About Andy?

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:34.300
-Nah. It'll be fun while it lasts.
-I'm proud of you, cowboy.

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:38.980
Besides, when it all ends, I'll have old
Buzz Lightyear to keep me company

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:41.700
for infinity and beyond.

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:46.140
♪ You're gonna see it's our destiny

00:06:48.620 --> 00:06:52.020
-♪ You've got a friend in me
-♪ Yes, you do

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:55.540
-♪ You've got a friend in me
-♪ That's the truth

00:06:55.980 --> 00:06:58.220
♪ You've got a friend

00:06:58.300 --> 00:07:03.460
♪ In me ♪

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:06.180
Yeah!

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:09.420
MAN 1: Speed.
MAN 2: Marker.

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:10.860
MAN 3: And action.

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:14.740
(GROANING, LAUGHING)

00:07:15.460 --> 00:07:18.020
(STRUGGLING, LAUGHING)

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:21.820
Okay. (SNORTING)
A little help here, please.

